Lab: Manage Storage for Application Configuration and Data
Goal
Deploy a web application and database that:
•	Share database credentials via a secret
•	Use local storage for database (better performance)
•	Use NFS storage for file-sharing apps (shareable)
•	Use ConfigMap to provide configuration files
•	Demonstrate adding/removing volumes and connecting apps
________________________________________
Step 1 — Login & Project
oc login -u developer -p developer https://api.ocp4.example.com:6443
oc project storage-review
________________________________________
Step 2 — Create Secret for DB Credentials
oc create secret generic world-cred \
  --from-literal user=redhat \
  --from-literal password=redhat123 \
  --from-literal database=world_x
Verify:
oc get secrets world-cred
________________________________________
Step 3 — Create ConfigMap for SQL file
oc create configmap dbfiles \
  --from-file ~/DO180/labs/storage-review/insertdata.sql
Verify:
oc get configmaps
________________________________________
Step 4 — Deploy Database
Create deployment:
oc create deployment dbserver \
  --image registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/redhattraining/mysql-app:v1
Set environment variables from secret:
oc set env deployment/dbserver --from secret/world-cred --prefix MYSQL_
Verify pod is RUNNING:
oc get pods
________________________________________
Step 5 — Add Persistent Volume to DB
oc set volume deployment/dbserver \
  --add --name dbserver-lvm --type persistentVolumeClaim \
  --claim-mode rwo --claim-size 1Gi \
  --mount-path /var/lib/mysql --claim-class lvms-vg1 \
  --claim-name dbserver-lvm-pvc
Check PVC:
oc get pvc
________________________________________
Step 6 — Expose DB Service
oc expose deployment dbserver --name mysql-service --port 3306 --target-port 3306
oc get services
oc get endpoints
________________________________________
Step 7 — Deploy Web Application (File Sharing)
Create deployment:
oc create deployment file-sharing \
  --image registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/redhattraining/php-webapp-mysql:v1
Scale to 2 replicas:
oc scale deployment file-sharing --replicas 2
Expose deployment:
oc expose deployment file-sharing --name file-sharing --port 8080 --target-port 8080
oc expose service/file-sharing
oc get routes
Test in browser:
http://file-sharing-storage-review.apps.ocp4.example.com
________________________________________
Step 8 — Mount ConfigMap to Web App
Mount dbfiles SQL file:
oc set volume deployment/file-sharing \
  --add --name=config-map-pvc \
  --type=configmap --configmap-name=dbfiles \
  --mount-path=/home/database-files
Verify content:
oc exec -it pod/file-sharing-XXXXX -- ls /home/database-files/
________________________________________
Step 9 — Add Shared NFS Volume to Web App
oc set volume deployment/file-sharing \
  --add --name shared-volume --type persistentVolumeClaim \
  --claim-mode rwo --claim-size 1Gi \
  --mount-path /home/sharedfiles --claim-class nfs-storage \
  --claim-name shared-pvc
Verify PVC:
oc get pvc
Copy SQL file to shared folder:
oc exec -it pod/file-sharing-XXXXX -- cp /home/database-files/insertdata.sql /home/sharedfiles/
oc exec -it pod/file-sharing-XXXXX -- ls /home/sharedfiles/
Remove ConfigMap volume:
oc set volume deployment/file-sharing --remove --name=config-map-pvc
________________________________________
Step 10 — Mount Shared Volume to DB
oc set volume deployment/dbserver \
  --add --name shared-volume \
  --claim-name shared-pvc \
  --mount-path /home/sharedfiles
Verify pod and content:
oc exec -it pod/dbserver-XXXXX -- head /home/sharedfiles/insertdata.sql
________________________________________
Step 11 — Load Data into Database
oc rsh dbserver-XXXXX
mysql -u$MYSQL_USER -p$MYSQL_PASSWORD world_x < /home/sharedfiles/insertdata.sql
exit
Verify web app connectivity in browser:
http://file-sharing-storage-review.apps.ocp4.example.com
________________________________________
Step 12 — Lab Completion
Grade your work:
lab grade storage-review
Finish lab:
lab finish storage-review
________________________________________
Key Concepts / Exam Points
Concept	Notes
Secret	Stores DB credentials, accessed via environment variables
ConfigMap	Provides configuration files (SQL) to pods
PVC	Persistent storage for data and shared files
Storage Class	lvms-vg1 (local), nfs-storage (shareable)
Web App Scaling	NFS allows sharing files across replicas
Volumes	Add/remove dynamically with oc set volume
Service & Route	Expose pods internally (service) and externally (route)

